            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0385" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.42/84: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-15T11:00:00+03:25">October 15, 1941—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:16 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>190. The Minister of Education informs me that he has invited Doctor Paul Monroe
                    of Columbia University to come to Iran as head of a commission to make a survey
                    of Iran’s educational problem. He <pb facs="0386" n="378" xml:id="pg378"/>
                    stated that he would appreciate the Department’s assistance in enlisting Doctor
                    Paul’s cooperation.</p>
                <p>I am of the opinion that such a commission would have a good effect on
                    American-Iranian relations and that the idea should be encouraged if the
                    Department feels such a course is wise under present conditions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
